WEBVTT

00:00.597 --> 00:03.836
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:03.936 --> 00:07.338
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.373 --> 00:10.774
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.810 --> 00:13.777
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.813 --> 00:17.381
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.416 --> 00:20.784
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.820 --> 00:22.353
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.388 --> 00:24.421
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.457 --> 00:25.360
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:33.866 --> 00:36.467
We now return to Hotel TV,

00:36.502 --> 00:38.836
the station that makes you feel
like you're at a hotel

00:38.871 --> 00:40.571
when you're not at a hotel.

00:40.606 --> 00:43.140
Have a romantic drink
by the concourse fountain.

00:43.175 --> 00:45.809
Or you can watch the big game
at Chopper's Bar and Grill,

00:45.845 --> 00:47.978
where they'll be pouring
till 2:00 a.m.

00:48.014 --> 00:49.480
Or maybe you're in the mood
for something

00:49.515 --> 00:50.781
a little more exotic.

00:50.816 --> 00:52.850
Try Jose Gato's
Brazilian Steakhouse.

00:52.885 --> 00:54.852
With rooftop views,
plus a fine selection

00:54.887 --> 00:56.253
of blended rum drinks.

00:56.288 --> 00:57.755
At the end of the night,

00:57.790 --> 00:59.256
<i>you won't want to say,
"Boa noite."</i>

00:59.291 --> 01:01.692
And you won't have to,
'cause Chopper's is open,

01:01.727 --> 01:03.594
where they're pouring
till 2:00 a.m.

01:03.629 --> 01:05.162
Should we go
to Chopper's?

01:05.197 --> 01:06.397
We interrupt this program

01:06.432 --> 01:08.732
to bring you a Chanel 5 News
special report.

01:08.768 --> 01:10.734
Good evening, Quahog.
I'm Tom Tucker.

01:10.770 --> 01:12.369
Tragedy stuck Haiti today

01:12.405 --> 01:14.905
as the island nation was rocked
by a major earthquake,

01:14.940 --> 01:17.107
leaving thousands dead
and injured.

01:18.277 --> 01:20.711
Coming up, local newsman
shows a camera operator

01:20.746 --> 01:22.846
how to center a shot.

01:22.882 --> 01:24.048
There we go.

01:24.083 --> 01:25.416
There, there's Tom.

01:25.451 --> 01:26.950
There's the star.

01:26.986 --> 01:28.986
Oh, my God.
That's terrible about Haiti.

01:29.021 --> 01:30.721
We got to do
something to help.

01:30.756 --> 01:32.056
No, we don't.

01:32.091 --> 01:33.791
Relax.
I'm sure Wyclef Jean

01:33.826 --> 01:35.392
has got it all under control.

01:35.428 --> 01:36.593
I've always talked about

01:36.629 --> 01:38.095
wanting to help in
these situations,

01:38.130 --> 01:39.797
but I never
follow through.

01:39.832 --> 01:42.099
Well, this time, I'm
really gonna do it.

01:42.134 --> 01:43.600
I'm gonna start
a blood drive.

01:43.636 --> 01:44.868
Good for you, Lois.

01:44.904 --> 01:46.937
You'll be a local hero,
like Paul Revere.

01:46.972 --> 01:48.572
The British will
be here soon.

01:48.607 --> 01:50.040
We shall stand our ground

01:50.076 --> 01:51.442
and fight them to the death!

01:51.477 --> 01:53.143
Yes! Yes!

01:53.179 --> 01:54.545
Although...
I mean, one of us

01:54.580 --> 01:55.746
should probably
warn everyone.

01:55.781 --> 01:57.281
You know... that the
British are coming.

01:57.316 --> 01:58.348
I mean, not me.

01:58.384 --> 01:59.616
I mean,
I want to fight.

01:59.652 --> 02:01.618
I mean, oh, shoot...
I've got the horse.

02:01.654 --> 02:03.821
I mean, but if
anyone else wants to go?

02:03.856 --> 02:04.856
I'll go.

02:04.857 --> 02:05.989
No one?
All right.

02:06.025 --> 02:08.192
I'll make sure everyone
remembers your names!

02:15.534 --> 02:17.468
Wow, Lois, you really
got a great turnout

02:17.503 --> 02:18.902
for the blood drive.
Oh, yeah.

02:18.938 --> 02:20.537
The whole thing's going off
without a hitch.

02:20.573 --> 02:21.939
Well, except
for that mosquito

02:21.974 --> 02:23.707
who keeps trying
to sneak in.

02:23.742 --> 02:25.008
Hi. I'm the new nurse.

02:25.044 --> 02:26.243
Get out of here!

02:26.278 --> 02:27.578
This blood's not for you!

02:27.613 --> 02:29.513
Aw...

02:29.548 --> 02:31.715
Oh, look, an empty tire
with some water in it.

02:31.750 --> 02:34.251
All right,
I'm happy again.

02:34.286 --> 02:36.086
I'm gonna go ahead
and thank you

02:36.122 --> 02:37.287
for donating
blood today.

02:37.323 --> 02:38.388
Donating?!

02:38.424 --> 02:39.790
I thought we were
getting paid!

02:42.061 --> 02:45.329
Peter, everyone else here
has donated except you.

02:45.364 --> 02:46.530
That's not true.

02:46.565 --> 02:47.798
That guy over there
didn't donate.

02:47.833 --> 02:49.500
That's still
you, Peter.

02:49.535 --> 02:51.235
Oh. Well, if I got to donate,

02:51.270 --> 02:52.603
he's got to donate, too.

02:52.638 --> 02:54.338
You, get in here!

02:55.674 --> 02:57.007
Sucker!

02:57.042 --> 02:58.375
Son of a bitch!

03:02.181 --> 03:04.715
Lois! Lois!

03:04.750 --> 03:05.849
Mommy!

03:05.885 --> 03:07.217
Stewie,
what's going on?

03:07.253 --> 03:08.719
You should be
asleep by now.

03:08.754 --> 03:10.420
I can't sleep, Brian.
Where's the woman?

03:10.456 --> 03:12.289
I need her to read me
a bedtime story.

03:12.324 --> 03:13.724
Oh, she's busy with
the blood drive.

03:13.759 --> 03:14.791
Maybe I can help.

03:14.827 --> 03:16.360
How about I read you
this book?

03:16.395 --> 03:18.061
<i>It's called
Apathetic George.</i>

03:18.097 --> 03:20.130
"George used to be
a curious monkey,

03:20.166 --> 03:21.798
"but after
a month in captivity,

03:21.834 --> 03:23.467
"all he did
was wait for food.

03:23.502 --> 03:25.335
"The zoo people
wanted him to mate,

03:25.371 --> 03:27.437
"but he lost interest
in that, too.

03:27.473 --> 03:29.306
"20 years
and millions of dollars

03:29.341 --> 03:31.041
in zoo revenue later,
he died."

03:31.076 --> 03:33.043
Okay, I've had enough.
All right, you know what,

03:33.078 --> 03:35.245
I know something that will help
you sleep. Wait here.

03:35.281 --> 03:37.447
Well, I hope so.
Because I've tried everything.

03:37.483 --> 03:39.650
Counting sheep,
thinking sleepy thoughts.

03:39.685 --> 03:41.752
I even hired the Sandman.

03:41.787 --> 03:43.687
Sand and sand and
sand and sand

03:43.722 --> 03:46.590
and sand and sand
and good night!

03:46.625 --> 03:48.458
Okay, I'll give you
a tiny bit of this.

03:48.494 --> 03:50.227
It should help you sleep.
What is it?

03:50.262 --> 03:51.995
It's cough syrup.
It's not really for kids,

03:52.031 --> 03:54.031
but a capful
is pretty harmless.

03:55.067 --> 03:56.366
Mmm.

03:56.402 --> 03:59.870
Oh, so this is what Lil Wayne
keeps almost dying from.

03:59.905 --> 04:02.139
Ah, this is so relaxing.

04:02.174 --> 04:03.874
I could get used to this.

04:03.909 --> 04:06.877
Like the way I got used to
wearing European diapers.

04:06.912 --> 04:08.245
Don't mind me.

04:08.280 --> 04:10.280
I'm just grabbing
a little cheese and vino.

04:13.319 --> 04:15.118
If anybody needs me,
I'll be poolside

04:15.154 --> 04:18.956
next to my weirdly hot
girlfriend with dark teeth.

04:23.762 --> 04:25.229
Well, Lois, I'm
done giving blood.

04:25.264 --> 04:26.430
Just ask this guy.

04:26.465 --> 04:27.764
Is true, Lois.

04:27.800 --> 04:29.299
I sucked him dry.

04:29.335 --> 04:31.235
He gave a blood
donation as well.

04:31.270 --> 04:33.237
Peter, knock it off.
Just give some blood,

04:33.272 --> 04:35.172
get your cookie
and be done with it.

04:35.207 --> 04:36.840
Cookie?
Yes, Peter.

04:36.875 --> 04:39.042
There are cookies
for everyone who donates.

04:39.078 --> 04:40.477
Well, I already ate
two wedding cakes,

04:40.512 --> 04:42.346
but I guess I could
go for a cookie.

04:42.381 --> 04:43.480
All right, I'll do it.

04:43.515 --> 04:45.549
Peter, you're doing
a good thing.

04:45.584 --> 04:47.751
Thanks, Lois, but you got
to promise you'll warn me

04:47.786 --> 04:49.353
before they stick
that needle in me.

04:49.388 --> 04:51.622
Actually, we
just finished.

04:51.657 --> 04:53.557
Wow, that wasn't so bad.

04:53.592 --> 04:56.226
See, Peter? And now
you can have a cookie.

04:56.262 --> 04:57.694
Oh, awesome!

04:57.730 --> 05:01.298
Mmm. Mmm. Oh, my God,
Th-these are delicious.

05:01.333 --> 05:02.966
Lois, you made these?

05:03.002 --> 05:05.435
Yeah, I found one
of my grandmother's old recipes,

05:05.471 --> 05:08.572
so I thought I'd make a special
batch for the blood drive.

05:08.607 --> 05:11.174
Well, I'm glad you did.
These cookies are amazing.

05:11.210 --> 05:14.177
They're even tastier
than Connie Britton's hair.

05:18.217 --> 05:20.384
Mmm. God, your
hair is delicious.

05:20.419 --> 05:21.852
Who are you?

05:21.887 --> 05:24.788
I'm the guy who killed
your bodyguard.

05:28.327 --> 05:30.227
Coming this fall
to every network,

05:30.262 --> 05:34.164
your favorite sitcom lines
preceded by the word "uh."

05:34.199 --> 05:36.166
Uh, knock much?

05:38.871 --> 05:41.505
Uh, that just happened.

05:43.709 --> 05:46.343
Uh, so I guess this
is a thing now?

05:46.378 --> 05:48.345
Uh, yeah, no.

05:48.380 --> 05:50.280
Uh, awkward.

05:51.717 --> 05:54.685
<i>TV, that thing
you used to watch.</i>

05:54.720 --> 05:56.186
Oh, these are incredible.

05:56.221 --> 05:57.454
Hey, you know something?

05:57.489 --> 05:59.723
If we sold these, we could
make a ton of money.

05:59.758 --> 06:01.491
Maybe we should open
our own cookie store.

06:01.527 --> 06:03.627
Are you serious?
Yeah, why not?

06:03.662 --> 06:05.595
I mean, if George Foreman
can make electric grills,

06:05.631 --> 06:06.997
we can do this.

06:07.032 --> 06:09.266
I mean, I've seen that guy
get punched in the face

06:09.301 --> 06:11.201
a thousand times, and now
he's making science stuff.

06:11.236 --> 06:13.603
Who'd think that idiot
would still be walking around

06:13.639 --> 06:15.972
and Muhammad Ali
can't even talk anymore?

06:16.008 --> 06:18.508
You know, having our own store
could be kind of fun.

06:18.544 --> 06:20.544
And you'd really do it with me?

06:20.579 --> 06:21.812
Absolutely.

06:21.847 --> 06:25.349
Oh, Peter, that actually sounds
kind of romantic.

06:25.384 --> 06:28.952
I always wanted you and me
to work on a project together.

06:28.987 --> 06:30.687
Oh, let's do it!

06:30.723 --> 06:33.290
All right! Now, let's
turn up the TV real loud

06:33.325 --> 06:36.093
so the kids can't
hear us having sex.

06:36.128 --> 06:37.894
Aah! Aah!

06:37.930 --> 06:40.831
Sex! Sex!

06:46.920 --> 06:49.220
There's my handsome
business partner.

06:49.256 --> 06:51.757
Now, we can't be late for
our meeting with the bank.

06:51.792 --> 06:54.226
That's so cool you guys
are gonna open a business.

06:54.261 --> 06:56.428
Yeah, well, I got a ton
of business experience.

06:56.464 --> 06:58.097
I mean, I had that job
creating ads

06:58.132 --> 07:00.399
for the North Dakota
board of tourism.

07:00.434 --> 07:02.067
<i>Hi. Do you like South Dakota</i>

07:02.103 --> 07:03.902
<i>but don't want
to see Mount Rushmore?</i>

07:03.938 --> 07:05.371
<i>Come to North Dakota.</i>

07:05.406 --> 07:07.773
<i>It's just a very long drive
from wherever you live.</i>

07:07.808 --> 07:09.875
<i>Best of all,
most of the good license plates</i>

07:09.910 --> 07:11.143
<i>aren't taken yet.</i>

07:11.178 --> 07:13.746
<i>Imagine coming here
and having "Cool Dude"</i>

07:13.781 --> 07:15.748
<i>or "Yay Jews"</i>

07:15.783 --> 07:17.583
<i>or "Boo Jews,"</i>

07:17.618 --> 07:19.785
<i>depending on where you stand
on Jews.</i>

07:19.820 --> 07:22.721
<i>North Dakota.
We're not even the best Dakota.</i>

07:23.758 --> 07:25.391
Stewie,
what are you doing?

07:25.426 --> 07:27.926
Huh? Oh, Brian,
oh, there you are.

07:27.962 --> 07:30.929
I've been... I've been looking
all over the table for you.

07:30.965 --> 07:33.932
You know, I've got to tell
you, this stuff you gave me

07:33.968 --> 07:36.201
was a lifesaver
last night.

07:36.237 --> 07:37.903
I was out
like a light.

07:37.938 --> 07:40.906
And, you know, normally,
I'm up five or six times

07:40.941 --> 07:43.909
to scream and defecate.
But you know what?

07:43.944 --> 07:45.577
I slept straight
through.

07:45.613 --> 07:47.513
Stewie, I told you,
there's alcohol in that.

07:47.548 --> 07:49.081
It's not for kids.

07:49.116 --> 07:52.418
You're not for kids.

07:52.453 --> 07:54.420
Stewie, you're drunk.

07:54.455 --> 07:56.422
Oh, Brian's all serious.

07:56.457 --> 07:58.757
"Oh, I don't... I don't
drink in the morning

07:58.793 --> 08:00.392
because I've got
to land a plane."

08:01.695 --> 08:03.929
All right, come on, I've got
to drive you to daycare.

08:03.964 --> 08:06.932
Okay, okay, it's all right.
C-Calm down, calm down.

08:06.967 --> 08:08.934
Uh, uh, oh. Oh, I think I...

08:08.969 --> 08:12.037
I think I've put my shoes
on the wrong feet.

08:12.073 --> 08:14.006
Is it 9:15 already?

08:14.041 --> 08:16.041
Lois, we got to go!

08:22.483 --> 08:24.850
You know, I've got all
the papers for the loan officer,

08:24.885 --> 08:27.453
but, I got to admit,
I'm a little nervous.

08:27.488 --> 08:29.788
Don't worry, we're gonna
get this loan, no problem.

08:29.824 --> 08:32.057
And if you get nervous,
just do what I always do,

08:32.093 --> 08:33.725
picture your
audience naked.

08:33.761 --> 08:35.461
Good afternoon,
Mr. and Mrs. Griffin.

08:35.496 --> 08:37.796
Aah! Get that enormous
thing out of my face!

08:37.832 --> 08:40.466
I'll be your loan officer,
so why don't you have a seat

08:40.501 --> 08:42.167
and tell me
about your business.

08:42.203 --> 08:43.402
Our business
is cookies.

08:43.437 --> 08:44.903
Now let me ask
you a question.

08:44.939 --> 08:46.905
You ever heard of money?
Yes.

08:46.941 --> 08:48.907
Good, good. We're
on the same page.

08:48.943 --> 08:50.709
Now, sir, let me ask
you something else.

08:50.744 --> 08:54.046
Can you name one successful
company that isn't cookie-based?

08:54.081 --> 08:55.447
Microsoft.

08:55.483 --> 08:57.382
Peter, I'll handle this.

08:57.418 --> 09:00.119
Uh, my husband and I would like
to open a cookie store.

09:00.154 --> 09:01.453
We've done all the research,

09:01.489 --> 09:04.123
and I'm very confident
we can turn a profit.

09:04.158 --> 09:07.326
I've brought some samples
if you'd like to try one.

09:07.361 --> 09:08.927
She said one.

09:08.963 --> 09:10.963
Take one.

09:12.433 --> 09:15.067
Mmm. Well,
these are delicious.

09:15.102 --> 09:18.871
Let me just run this
by my supervisor.

09:18.906 --> 09:20.572
Yes!

09:20.608 --> 09:22.741
Mr. and Mrs. Griffin,
this bank would like

09:22.776 --> 09:24.276
to help you start
your business.

09:24.311 --> 09:26.945
Really?!
Oh, that's fantastic!

09:26.981 --> 09:28.480
And if you have
any other questions,

09:28.516 --> 09:31.350
you can call me
at any time.

09:33.454 --> 09:34.753
Hello?

09:34.788 --> 09:37.823
How far away are the stars?

09:43.130 --> 09:44.930
Brian! Brian!

09:44.965 --> 09:46.798
Hold-hold on one second.

09:46.834 --> 09:48.634
I'll be right with you,
Mr. Duckford.

09:48.669 --> 09:50.636
Brian!
What?

09:50.671 --> 09:54.173
Let's order... I was just
thinking, let's order a kebab.

09:54.208 --> 09:56.175
A what?
A kebab.

09:56.210 --> 09:58.177
But I... but I want it
in this order:

09:58.212 --> 10:00.179
vegetable, meat, meat,

10:00.214 --> 10:02.181
vegetable, meat.

10:02.216 --> 10:05.184
And, uh, Mr. Duckford
would like some quackers.

10:05.219 --> 10:07.519
Can I leave now?

10:07.555 --> 10:10.522
No, no, Bri... No, you can't.
Brian, I need your help.

10:10.558 --> 10:13.659
I've made a series
of small poops in my bath,

10:13.694 --> 10:16.328
and I need you to scoop them out
with this fishnet.

10:16.363 --> 10:18.330
Yeah, I'm not doing that.
You have to.

10:18.365 --> 10:20.232
You're my butler.
I'm not your butler.

10:20.267 --> 10:22.334
I know, but wouldn't
it be great if you were?

10:22.369 --> 10:24.336
It'd be... I'd be so happy.

10:24.371 --> 10:27.005
In fact, the only thing
that would make me happier is...

10:27.041 --> 10:30.342
would... is... would be if this
tub was filled with "yawgurt."

10:30.377 --> 10:32.477
Can you... can you get me
some yawgurt?

10:32.513 --> 10:34.479
Is the yawgurt shop
still open?

10:34.515 --> 10:37.349
Is there... is there some place
to dial up yawgurt?

10:37.384 --> 10:39.685
Stop saying that.
What's the best skin yawgurt?

10:39.720 --> 10:42.221
Who can... who can prepare me
a nice yawgurt treatment?

10:42.256 --> 10:44.890
If you say it like that one
more time, I'm gonna drown you.

10:44.925 --> 10:46.892
Yawgurt. Uh, see?

10:46.927 --> 10:48.894
You're not... you're not
gonna do anything.

10:48.929 --> 10:53.232
Hey, hey, Brian,
am I a good little guy?

10:56.837 --> 10:59.071
This space
will be perfect, Peter.

10:59.106 --> 11:00.272
Yeah, it sure will, Lois.

11:00.307 --> 11:02.341
Now all we got to do
is name the store.

11:02.376 --> 11:03.575
Ooh, ooh, I got it.

11:03.611 --> 11:04.943
Peter's Wife's Cookies.

11:04.979 --> 11:06.378
I love it.

11:06.413 --> 11:07.679
And I love you.

11:07.715 --> 11:09.248
Really?
Yes.

11:09.283 --> 11:11.450
You know, we did so-so
building a family,

11:11.485 --> 11:12.718
but this business--

11:12.753 --> 11:15.120
I think we can really
knock it out of the park.

11:15.155 --> 11:16.555
Oh, we sure can, Lois.

11:16.590 --> 11:17.889
We're gonna be a great team.

11:17.925 --> 11:20.859
Like Moses and his buddy who
liked to collect seashells.

11:25.065 --> 11:27.065
Yay!

11:34.174 --> 11:36.341
I can't believe it, Peter.

11:36.377 --> 11:37.976
Our first day
of business.

11:38.012 --> 11:39.511
All right. Well,
we have got work to do,

11:39.546 --> 11:41.613
so let's roll up our sleeves
and get right to it.

11:41.649 --> 11:43.315
There's a lot to do,
so we can't be afraid

11:43.350 --> 11:45.284
to just roll up our sleeves
and get the job done.

11:45.319 --> 11:46.818
We can't be hands-off managers.

11:46.854 --> 11:48.820
We got to roll up our sleeves
and just dig in.

11:48.856 --> 11:50.656
Peter, your arms
are turning purple.

11:50.691 --> 11:53.258
Purple with success.
That's the color of money.

11:53.294 --> 11:55.694
You got to do the work of two
men and pay yourself for one.

11:55.729 --> 11:58.096
Just roll up those sleeves
and address the task at hand,

11:58.132 --> 12:00.365
whatever it may be, not shying
away from the dirty work,

12:00.401 --> 12:02.501
but just rolling up our sleeves
and having at it.

12:02.536 --> 12:04.403
Success is not given.
It is taken.

12:04.438 --> 12:07.172
It's time to get in the game
and get dirty.

12:07.207 --> 12:09.207
All right, I'm going to lunch.

12:14.381 --> 12:16.281
Uh, yes, I'd like
a chocolate chip cookie.

12:16.317 --> 12:17.582
Elmer!

12:17.618 --> 12:19.584
What, Mom? You promised
I could get a cookie

12:19.620 --> 12:20.886
if I finished
all my surgery.

12:20.921 --> 12:22.254
Did you?

12:22.289 --> 12:23.889
Yeah.
All of it?

12:23.924 --> 12:26.325
Um...
Get back there.

12:26.360 --> 12:27.526
I'm gonna do it.

12:27.561 --> 12:30.162
What does it matter
when I do it?

12:35.536 --> 12:37.269
Lois, Lois, lock the door.
Why?

12:37.304 --> 12:39.137
It's that lady who comes
in, tries a sample,

12:39.173 --> 12:41.606
and then whispers about
how bad she is. Hey.

12:41.642 --> 12:44.476
Oh, my God, you have
chocolate macadamia nut?

12:44.511 --> 12:46.411
Oh, could I just try
a little sample?

12:46.447 --> 12:48.547
Oh, I'm so bad.

12:48.582 --> 12:49.981
Uh, sure.

12:50.017 --> 12:51.516
You gonna buy a
cookie this time?

12:51.552 --> 12:54.286
Oh, I better just
stick with the sample.

12:54.321 --> 12:55.587
I'm so bad.

12:55.622 --> 12:57.055
But at least
I know I'm bad,

12:57.091 --> 12:59.191
so that makes me
a little less bad.

12:59.226 --> 13:00.492
Or worse.

13:01.528 --> 13:04.296
That was the right thing
to do, Peter.

13:08.836 --> 13:10.535
Oh, boy, it's been
really slow.

13:10.571 --> 13:12.404
I mean, if it doesn't
pick up soon,

13:12.439 --> 13:14.473
we're not gonna stay
in business very long.

13:14.508 --> 13:16.341
Don't you worry,
Lois, you keep baking,

13:16.377 --> 13:17.776
I'll drum up some business.

13:17.811 --> 13:19.578
We just got to think
outside the box,

13:19.613 --> 13:21.947
like the makers of
Dreyer's ice cream.

13:21.982 --> 13:24.282
Guys, I've said it before,
and I'll say it again:

13:24.318 --> 13:25.817
When people go to
the supermarket,

13:25.853 --> 13:27.185
they need something
to look at

13:27.221 --> 13:29.454
before they choose
Haagen-Dazs.

13:35.462 --> 13:37.896
Hey, dude, can you pass me
a speck of Spazz?

13:37.931 --> 13:39.364
Sorry, brah,
all out.

13:39.400 --> 13:41.066
You want a cube
of Froosh?

13:41.101 --> 13:42.768
Nah, I'm not into Froosh.

13:42.803 --> 13:44.770
I got a tear
of Laser Dragon.

13:44.805 --> 13:46.037
Can I handle it?

13:46.073 --> 13:48.507
I don't know.
Can you?

13:48.542 --> 13:51.276
Gum! What the hell is going on?!

13:51.311 --> 13:53.311
I don't know
what to do, you guys.

13:53.347 --> 13:55.046
The cookie shop
is tanking.

13:55.082 --> 13:56.281
If it fails,
we're screwed.

13:56.316 --> 13:57.549
My God,
what does it take

13:57.584 --> 13:59.418
to get people
to buy a damn cookie?

13:59.453 --> 14:00.786
Peter, let me
tell you something.

14:00.821 --> 14:02.487
I spend $600 a month

14:02.523 --> 14:04.356
on scented candles
at the farmer's market

14:04.391 --> 14:06.024
just because there's
a hot chick selling them.

14:06.059 --> 14:07.292
So what are you saying?

14:07.327 --> 14:08.794
You just bragging
about candles?

14:08.829 --> 14:10.262
That's a weird thing
to brag about.

14:10.297 --> 14:11.797
No, I'm saying
sex sells.

14:11.832 --> 14:13.265
Trust me,
you get a few hotties

14:13.300 --> 14:14.533
in that cookie shop
of yours,

14:14.568 --> 14:16.435
I bet your sales
will go up.

14:16.470 --> 14:17.736
Giggity.

14:17.771 --> 14:19.771
That was an unearned
giggity, Quagmire.

14:19.807 --> 14:20.972
I said "up."

14:21.008 --> 14:22.174
No?

14:22.209 --> 14:23.375
No.
No.

14:23.410 --> 14:25.110
Well, I'll try
anything, Quagmire,

14:25.145 --> 14:26.845
'cause I actually like
running that cookie shop.

14:26.880 --> 14:28.513
It's way better
than that job I had

14:28.549 --> 14:30.482
telemarketing
to buttholes.

14:30.517 --> 14:31.883
Hello?

14:31.919 --> 14:33.084
Sorry, wrong number.

14:33.120 --> 14:34.286
Hello?

14:34.321 --> 14:36.021
Sorry, wrong number.

14:37.291 --> 14:39.491
And how are you today, sir?

14:43.530 --> 14:45.397
Oh, my God.

14:45.432 --> 14:47.499
Customers.

14:49.303 --> 14:50.936
What the hell?

14:54.675 --> 14:56.274
Peter, what did you do?

14:56.310 --> 14:58.009
I saved our business.

14:58.045 --> 14:59.511
And don't worry,
I only hired women

14:59.546 --> 15:01.112
whose names are
cookie-related.

15:01.148 --> 15:03.148
Lois, meet
Cookie, Sugar,

15:03.183 --> 15:05.150
Spice, Cinnamon,
Brown Sugar

15:05.185 --> 15:06.351
and Butter.

15:06.386 --> 15:07.986
Oh, hey,
Butter.

15:08.021 --> 15:09.654
Some guys
like Butter.

15:16.416 --> 15:18.945
Peter, you turned our store
into a strip club.

15:18.945 --> 15:20.978
And I don't like
what this place has become.

15:21.013 --> 15:22.946
You mean hugely
profitable?

15:22.981 --> 15:24.915
We made all that today?

15:24.950 --> 15:26.216
Well, it was
twice as much,

15:26.251 --> 15:28.018
but I had to bail out
Cinnamon's kid.

15:28.053 --> 15:29.720
Thanks, Mr. Peter.

15:29.755 --> 15:32.456
This guy's the best.

15:32.491 --> 15:35.826
Well, I guess business
is better than ever.

15:35.861 --> 15:37.427
That's the spirit, Lois.

15:37.463 --> 15:39.296
Just you watch, we'll
be a bigger success

15:39.331 --> 15:41.098
than Richard Branson.

15:41.133 --> 15:43.400
Hey, where's the business
guy in this boardroom?

15:43.435 --> 15:45.635
It couldn't be that
tan, long-haired guy

15:45.671 --> 15:47.604
with the white linen
pants, could it?

15:47.639 --> 15:48.905
It is!

15:48.941 --> 15:51.942
And now, to my amphibious
sky submarine.

15:53.145 --> 15:56.747
I have way too much money!

16:04.790 --> 16:06.757
Come on, get-get down there,

16:06.792 --> 16:08.492
you old bag.

16:09.995 --> 16:11.895
There we go.

16:13.399 --> 16:14.664
Stewie, what are you doing?

16:14.700 --> 16:16.433
Being awesome.

16:19.004 --> 16:20.170
Whoa, whoa,
wait, wait.

16:20.205 --> 16:21.905
You're in no
condition to drive.

16:21.940 --> 16:24.508
I'm fine to drive.
I'm so fine.

16:24.543 --> 16:26.343
You s...
I can do all the tests.

16:26.378 --> 16:28.245
See?
I can touch my nose.

16:29.515 --> 16:30.814
I can touch my...

16:30.849 --> 16:33.316
♪ Head, shoulder, knees
and toes, knees and toes. ♪

16:33.352 --> 16:34.518
Stop it.

16:34.553 --> 16:35.819
No, you stop it.

16:35.854 --> 16:37.154
You stop it, Brian.

16:37.189 --> 16:38.221
You're interfering

16:38.257 --> 16:40.257
with my professional
business.

16:42.327 --> 16:44.161
Where's the radio?

16:46.365 --> 16:48.432
Oh, my God, are you okay?

16:48.467 --> 16:50.934
No. I don't feel so good.

16:50.969 --> 16:53.637
We should probably
exchange numbers.

16:53.672 --> 16:55.939
Okay. I'm a ten,
you're a four.

17:07.820 --> 17:11.188
This one's our new
chocolate white chocolate,

17:11.223 --> 17:13.056
and for every
dozen we sell,

17:13.091 --> 17:14.991
we donate 50 cents

17:15.027 --> 17:17.194
to Operation Smile.

17:17.230 --> 17:18.396
Yeah, nobody's
listening to you.

17:18.430 --> 17:19.596
They're all watching Sugar

17:19.631 --> 17:21.431
write frosting
swears on her jugs.

17:22.668 --> 17:25.035
She just wrote
"vagina" on her boobs.

17:25.070 --> 17:26.670
That doesn't even
make any sense.

17:26.705 --> 17:27.971
She's doing what?

17:28.006 --> 17:29.272
I told her ten minutes ago

17:29.308 --> 17:31.141
to put another batch
of oatmeal in the oven.

17:31.176 --> 17:32.442
Oh, that dough
is gone, Lois.

17:32.478 --> 17:34.110
I warmed it up
and put it behind

17:34.146 --> 17:36.546
those waist-high
holes in the wall.

17:36.582 --> 17:38.782
Is it spaghetti?
A bowl of grapes?

17:38.817 --> 17:41.551
Ooh, this is the best
haunted house ever.

17:41.587 --> 17:43.487
Peter, this is disgusting.

17:43.522 --> 17:45.388
I know we made a few changes,

17:45.424 --> 17:48.558
but this store should
still be about selling cookies.

17:48.594 --> 17:51.061
Well, you're never gonna
sell any looking like that.

17:51.096 --> 17:53.263
There. Now you're
ready to sell cookies.

17:53.298 --> 17:54.464
You know what?

17:54.500 --> 17:56.766
That's it. I'm done.

17:56.802 --> 17:59.369
I don't know why I ever
let you talk me into this...

17:59.404 --> 18:01.204
this...
whatever this is now.

18:01.240 --> 18:03.540
It's a strip club that
gives away free cookies.

18:03.575 --> 18:05.542
Ugh.

18:17.656 --> 18:19.456
Oh, crap.

18:19.491 --> 18:20.991
I should've known
something was up

18:21.026 --> 18:23.226
when I saw all those
cars out front.

18:23.262 --> 18:25.161
Stewie, why don't you
come and have a seat

18:25.197 --> 18:26.763
with all your friends here?

18:26.798 --> 18:28.231
We have something
to say to you.

18:28.267 --> 18:29.633
I'll go first.

18:29.668 --> 18:32.402
"Stewie, I remember
the day you were born.

18:32.437 --> 18:34.271
"I thought to myself,
here's a kid

18:34.306 --> 18:35.839
"who's got a white,
empty canvas

18:35.874 --> 18:37.440
stretched out
in front of him."

18:37.476 --> 18:39.543
Oh, please.
What... Who...

18:39.578 --> 18:40.844
What is this...
What is this,

18:40.879 --> 18:42.779
the circle
of perfect people?

18:42.814 --> 18:44.247
Who are you
to judge me?

18:44.283 --> 18:46.182
Mis-Mister...
Mister Giraffe,

18:46.218 --> 18:49.319
who lets l-little boys
grind on his rump.

18:49.354 --> 18:52.989
Mr. Octopus, who lets
little boys grind on his rump.

18:53.025 --> 18:54.724
Every one of you
has your own problems.

18:54.760 --> 18:56.359
Yeah, but you're
the only one who almost

18:56.395 --> 18:57.761
killed a kid yesterday.

18:57.796 --> 18:59.462
Yeah, well, that's, d...
That's because that...

18:59.498 --> 19:01.431
'Cause, because that
kid... That's because...

19:01.466 --> 19:02.966
because that... 'ca...
because that kid...

19:03.001 --> 19:04.568
that kid...

19:04.603 --> 19:06.369
I know.

19:06.405 --> 19:07.671
Oh, Brian.

19:07.706 --> 19:09.005
Who am I?

19:09.041 --> 19:10.941
I don't have a cough,
and my sinuses

19:10.976 --> 19:12.943
are remarkably
wide open.

19:12.978 --> 19:14.344
But I have a problem.

19:14.379 --> 19:16.413
Good. Admitting it
is the first step.

19:16.448 --> 19:18.114
But don't worry,
I'll get you through it.

19:18.150 --> 19:19.316
Thank you, Brian.

19:19.351 --> 19:20.717
You're welcome, Stewie.

19:20.752 --> 19:23.219
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I have to go to Chris's room.

19:23.255 --> 19:24.721
We're doing
a masturbation intervention.

19:24.756 --> 19:27.891
I got a bunch of his friends
sitting in a circle in there...

19:27.926 --> 19:29.859
Oh, dear God.

19:34.700 --> 19:36.166
Oh. Hey.

19:36.201 --> 19:37.968
Lois, before you
say anything,

19:38.003 --> 19:39.843
there's something
important I want to tell you.

19:39.871 --> 19:42.205
After you left, I ate
cookie dough off the stomach

19:42.240 --> 19:43.640
of a 20-year-old,
and then I vomited

19:43.675 --> 19:45.075
and all the girls
laughed at me,

19:45.110 --> 19:47.744
and then it came out that they
all think I'm fat and old.

19:47.779 --> 19:48.945
Is that it?

19:48.981 --> 19:51.114
I guess what I'm trying
to say is...

19:51.149 --> 19:53.917
I was wrong to choose
sexiness over my wife.

19:54.987 --> 19:56.152
Peter, what are you doing?

19:56.188 --> 19:57.354
What-what was that?

19:57.389 --> 19:59.422
Oh, back at the store,
I, uh, tucked my boner

19:59.458 --> 20:02.025
into the waistband of my pants
and now it's sitting weird.

20:02.060 --> 20:03.693
That's your apology?

20:03.729 --> 20:06.496
Well, that and this.

20:10.636 --> 20:11.801
Oh, Peter, did...

20:11.837 --> 20:13.370
did you bake this?

20:13.405 --> 20:15.872
Yeah. I love you, Lois.

20:15.907 --> 20:17.540
I really liked
having a store with you,

20:17.576 --> 20:19.643
and I'm...
I'm sorry I messed it up.

20:19.678 --> 20:21.778
I was only trying to help.

20:21.813 --> 20:23.647
I know, Peter.

20:23.682 --> 20:25.882
So you want
to split this with me?

20:25.917 --> 20:28.051
Uh, I wouldn't.
Butter helped me with it,

20:28.086 --> 20:30.387
and she has
chlamydia fingers.

20:34.059 --> 20:36.159
Well, it was fun
having our own store.

20:36.194 --> 20:37.694
But from now on,
my cookies

20:37.729 --> 20:39.896
are only
for these customers.

20:39.931 --> 20:42.365
Oh, Mom.

20:42.401 --> 20:44.434
So, Mom, what are you
gonna do with the shop?

20:44.469 --> 20:45.869
Well, I talked
to the bank,

20:45.904 --> 20:48.038
and they agreed
to take it back.

20:48.073 --> 20:50.040
Me love Cookie. Om, nom, nom,
nom, nom, nom, nom, nom, nom...

20:50.075 --> 20:56.575
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru